' Guide - MVVM layers (explanatory diagram for the root README; not a C4 level or 4+1 view)
' Version 1.1 - 2026-10-20
' Same element names as the C4 and 4+1 diagrams. Each layer box lists the real classes in it.
' PokemonApi returns DTOs and CaughtPokemonDao returns entities; the repository converts both with the
' mappers in data.mapper, so the ViewModels only see domain models (Pokemon, PokemonSummary, ...).
@startuml mvvm
!include ../style.puml

title MVVM in the Pokédex app
left to right direction

rectangle "**View**\nJetpack Compose\n\nHomeScreen\nPokedexScreen\nPokemonDetailScreen" as View
rectangle "**ViewModel**\nLifecycle ViewModel + LiveData\n\nHomeViewModel\nPokedexViewModel\nPokemonDetailViewModel" as ViewModel
rectangle "**Model**\ndata layer\n\nPokemonRepository\n+ mappers (DTO, entity → domain)" as Repository
component "PokemonApi\n(Retrofit)" as PokemonApi
component "CaughtPokemonDao\n(Room)" as Dao
component "PokeAPI" <<external>> as PokeAPI
database "Local Database\n(pokedex.db)" as LocalDb

View --> ViewModel : user events\n(onQueryChange, toggleType,\ntoggleCaught)
View <.. ViewModel : UI state\n(LiveData, observeAsState)
ViewModel --> Repository : suspend calls\n(viewModelScope)
ViewModel <.. Repository : domain models,\nRoom LiveData
Repository --> PokemonApi : fetch (DTOs)
Repository --> Dao : read / write (entities)
PokemonApi --> PokeAPI : HTTPS/JSON
Dao --> LocalDb : SQLite

note bottom of ViewModel
  Hilt creates each ViewModel
  (hiltViewModel()) and injects
  PokemonRepository.
end note
@enduml
